-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions of seat gpai from part P0 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P0-cases-seat-gpai: the cases of the questions in P0-seat-gpai.l4: the facts a person in the seat would state.
-- Every expected value was decided from the text of the Regulation before the file was run and is written beside its assertion with the words that license it;
-- none was copied from the encoding's output. A failing assertion is a finding, never an expectation to edit.
-- Dates the cases stand on: 31 July 2024 (the day before entry into force), 1 August 2024, 1 and 2 February 2025 (Chapter I), 26 and 27 July 2026 (each side of the Omnibus),
-- 1 and 2 August 2026 (the general date), 2 December 2026, 2 August 2027, 2 December 2027, 2 August 2028, 2 August 2030, 31 December 2030, as each function needs.
-- A MIRROR comment marks a case whose facts are asked, with the same answer, in the case file of another seat (the Guide, section 3).
-- A #TRACE is preceded by its -- EXPECT line (FULFILLED, BREACH or OPEN: the obligation still pending). The clock of a trace is the number of days since the day the rule counts from.
-- Assertions: 67. Traces: 5.

§ `Article 1: does Chapter I apply on the date asked?`

-- Under Article 1, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does Chapter I apply on the date asked
-- 1 January 2024, before the Regulation exists: JUST FALSE, the Regulation has not entered into force (Art 113, first paragraph: "on the twentieth day following that of its publication")
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 1 1 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 31 July 2024, the day before entry into force: JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 31 7 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 1 August 2024, in force but Chapter I applies only from 2 February 2025: JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 1 8 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 1 February 2025, the day before Chapter I applies (Art 113(a)): JUST FALSE
-- MIRROR Art 113(a): whether Chapter I applies, asked from every seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 1 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, the day Chapter I applies (Art 113(a)): JUST TRUE
-- MIRROR Art 113(a): whether Chapter I applies, asked from every seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 2 2 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 26 July 2026, the text as enacted still in force: JUST TRUE (as enacted point (a): "Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 26 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST TRUE (point (a) as replaced keeps 2 February 2025 for Chapters I and II)
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 27 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE


§ `Article 2(1): does the Regulation apply to me?`

-- Under Article 2(1)(a), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to me
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(a), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to me` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, the party places a general-purpose AI model on the Union market: JUST TRUE ("providers placing on the market or putting into service AI systems or placing on the market general-purpose AI models in the Union, irrespective of whether those providers are established or located within the Union or in a third country")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(a), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to me` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 2 February 2025, nothing placed in the Union: NOTHING (the paragraph names those who place; it does not say the Regulation applies to no one else)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(a), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to me` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: the same, JUST TRUE (paragraph 1 was not changed)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(a), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to me` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 31 July 2024, before entry into force: NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(a), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to me` (Date 31 7 2024) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING


§ `Article 2(6): AI systems and models developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development`

-- Under Article 2(6), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to the AI model developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(6), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to the AI model developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, specifically developed and put into service for research alone: JUST FALSE ("This Regulation does not apply to AI systems or AI models, including their output, specifically developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(6), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to the AI model developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, not for the sole purpose: NOTHING (limited by "for the sole purpose")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(6), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to the AI model developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, not specifically developed and put into service for research: NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(6), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to the AI model developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST FALSE (paragraph 6 was not changed)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(6), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to the AI model developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE


§ `Article 2(8): research, testing and development before placing on the market`

-- Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to my research, testing or development activity
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to my research, testing or development activity` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, research, testing or development before placing on the market, not in real world conditions: JUST FALSE ("This Regulation does not apply to any research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models prior to their being placed on the market or put into service")
-- MIRROR Art 2(8): research, testing or development before placing on the market, asked from the provider seat and the model provider seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to my research, testing or development activity` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, testing in real world conditions: NOTHING ("Testing in real world conditions shall not be covered by that exclusion")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to my research, testing or development activity` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, not before placing on the market or putting into service: NOTHING (limited by "prior to their being placed on the market")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to my research, testing or development activity` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, not a research, testing or development activity: NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to my research, testing or development activity` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST FALSE (paragraph 8 was not changed)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to my research, testing or development activity` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, must my research, testing or development activity be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, must my research, testing or development activity be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, an excluded activity: JUST TRUE ("Such activities shall be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law")
-- MIRROR Art 2(8) second sentence: the duty to follow applicable Union law, asked from the provider seat and the model provider seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, must my research, testing or development activity be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 2 February 2025, testing in real world conditions: NOTHING ("Such activities" are the excluded ones, and real world testing is not excluded)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, must my research, testing or development activity be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, not before placing on the market: NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, must my research, testing or development activity be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, not a research, testing or development activity: NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, must my research, testing or development activity be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING


§ `Article 3(3) to (8): does the definition of my role fit me?`

-- Under Article 3(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the definition of a provider fit me
-- develops it, places it on the market under its own name: TRUE ("develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model ... and places it on the market ... under its own name or trademark")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the definition of a provider fit me` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- has it developed by someone else and places it under its own name: TRUE ("or that has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the definition of a provider fit me` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- develops it and has it developed, places it under its own name: TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the definition of a provider fit me` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- develops it but does not place it on the market: FALSE (the definition says "means")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the definition of a provider fit me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- develops it and places it, but not under its own name or trademark: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the definition of a provider fit me` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- neither develops it nor has it developed: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the definition of a provider fit me` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Under Article 3(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, am I an operator
-- the seat's role is passed as the keel's `Role`: TRUE ("'operator' means a provider, product manufacturer, deployer, authorised representative, importer or distributor"): the role of this seat is on the list
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, am I an operator` EQUALS TRUE


§ `Article 3(9) to (11): placing on the market, making available on the market, putting into service`

-- Under Article 3(9), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my supply of the general-purpose AI model a placing on the market
-- a first making available on the Union market: TRUE ("the first making available of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model on the Union market")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(9), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my supply of the general-purpose AI model a placing on the market` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- a making available that is not the first: FALSE (the definition says "means")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(9), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my supply of the general-purpose AI model a placing on the market` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- not a making available on the Union market: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(9), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my supply of the general-purpose AI model a placing on the market` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE


