-- MIRROR Art 3(14a): the same enterprise asked from the provider, deployer and model provider seats
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(14a), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, am I a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise` (Date 27 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under Article 3(14b), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, am I a small mid-cap enterprise
-- 26 July 2026 (text as enacted), a small mid-cap enterprise: NOTHING (point (14b) is not in the text as enacted)
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(14b), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, am I a small mid-cap enterprise` (Date 26 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 26 July 2026, not one: NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(14b), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, am I a small mid-cap enterprise` (Date 26 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026 (text as amended), a small mid-cap enterprise: JUST TRUE ('small mid-cap enterprise' or 'SMC' means a small mid-cap enterprise as defined in point (2) of the Annex to Recommendation (EU) 2025/1099)
-- MIRROR Art 3(14b): the same enterprise asked from the provider, deployer and model provider seats
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(14b), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, am I a small mid-cap enterprise` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 27 July 2026, not one: JUST FALSE (the definition says "means")
-- MIRROR Art 3(14b): the same enterprise asked from the provider, deployer and model provider seats
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(14b), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, am I a small mid-cap enterprise` (Date 27 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE


§ `Article 3(63): is my model a general-purpose AI model?`

-- Under Article 3(63), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my model a general-purpose AI model
-- an AI model with significant generality, a wide range of tasks and integration, not used only for research before placing on the market: TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(63), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my model a general-purpose AI model` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- not an AI model: FALSE (the definition says "means")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(63), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my model a general-purpose AI model` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- no significant generality: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(63), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my model a general-purpose AI model` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- not capable of competently performing a wide range of distinct tasks: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(63), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my model a general-purpose AI model` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- cannot be integrated into a variety of downstream systems or applications: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(63), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my model a general-purpose AI model` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- used for research, development or prototyping before it is placed on the market: FALSE ("except AI models that are used for research, development or prototyping activities before they are placed on the market")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(63), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my model a general-purpose AI model` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE


§ `Article 111(3): general-purpose AI models already on the market`

-- Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, by what date must I take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation
-- 31 July 2024, before entry into force: NOTHING (the Regulation did not exist)
#ASSERT `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, by what date must I take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation` (Date 31 7 2024) (Date 1 1 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 1 August 2024, a model placed on 1 January 2024: JUST 2 August 2027 ("Providers of general-purpose AI models that have been placed on the market before 2 August 2025 shall take the necessary steps in order to comply with the obligations laid down in this Regulation by 2 August 2027")
#ASSERT `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, by what date must I take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation` (Date 1 8 2024) (Date 1 1 2024) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 8 2027)
-- 2 February 2025, a model placed on 1 August 2025, the day before the bound: JUST 2 August 2027 ("before 2 August 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, by what date must I take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation` (Date 2 2 2025) (Date 1 8 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 8 2027)
-- 2 February 2026, a model placed on 2 August 2025, the bound itself: NOTHING (not "before 2 August 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, by what date must I take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation` (Date 2 2 2026) (Date 2 8 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 26 July 2026, the text as enacted, a model placed on 1 August 2025: JUST 2 August 2027
#ASSERT `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, by what date must I take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation` (Date 26 7 2026) (Date 1 8 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 8 2027)
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST 2 August 2027 (paragraph 3 was not changed)
#ASSERT `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, by what date must I take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation` (Date 27 7 2026) (Date 1 8 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 8 2027)
-- 27 July 2026, a model placed on 3 August 2025: NOTHING (limited by "before 2 August 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, by what date must I take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation` (Date 27 7 2026) (Date 3 8 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 August 2026, the general date, a model placed on 1 August 2025: JUST 2 August 2027 (the date does not move on that day)
#ASSERT `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, by what date must I take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation` (Date 2 8 2026) (Date 1 8 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 8 2027)

-- Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, what must I do to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation on the date asked
-- a model placed on 1 August 2025: the provider takes the necessary steps on day 1096 (2 August 2027, counted from 1 August 2024): discharged
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, what must I do to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation on the date asked` (Date 1 8 2024) (Date 1 8 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Provider DOES `Art 111(3) take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in this Regulation` AT 1096
-- the same, one day late (3 August 2027): BREACH
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, what must I do to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation on the date asked` (Date 1 8 2024) (Date 1 8 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Provider DOES `Art 111(3) take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in this Regulation` AT 1097
-- the same, the provider does nothing and time passes beyond 2 August 2027: BREACH
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, what must I do to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation on the date asked` (Date 27 7 2026) (Date 1 8 2025) AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 1097
-- a model placed on 2 August 2025: nothing is owed, so a long wait is not a breach
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, what must I do to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation on the date asked` (Date 27 7 2026) (Date 2 8 2025) AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 1196
-- 31 July 2024, before the Regulation exists: nothing is owed
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, what must I do to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation on the date asked` (Date 31 7 2024) (Date 1 8 2025) AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 1196


